  "headline": "FDA's records show somatropin is not on the current shortage list; an earlier Novo Nordisk discontinuation was posted 2023-01-06 and is resolved",
  "headline_cites": ["D9"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21, somatropin is not on FDA's current shortage list; FDA's history shows an earlier shortage first posted on 2023-01-06 that has since been resolved.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The earlier posting was for Novo Nordisk, Inc. somatropin injection (package NDC 0169-7703-21) with status To Be Discontinued, initially posted 2025-11-14.",
      "cites": ["E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1167028 at Novo Nordisk A/S - KV ended 2021-11-18 and was classified VAI, 414 days before the 2023-01-06 shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1238387 at Novo Nordisk A/S - Hax ended 2023-06-01 and was classified VAI, 146 days after the 2023-01-06 shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1341150 at Novo Nordisk A/S - KV ended 2024-05-02 and was classified VAI, 482 days after the 2023-01-06 shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 2 days of somatropin 30 mg/3 mL 3 mL syringes on hand; Corvale General has 14.8 days and can spare 3 syringes while keeping two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked best option is to transfer 3 syringes of 30 mg/3 mL, 3 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to 3 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    }
  ]
}
